  "findings": [
    "S90D also reproduced a slow native root admission for the additional retained fixture: 1263.781 ms HTTPS, journal_begin 30.847 ms, worker 24.283 ms, journal_finish 1129.298 ms, handler 1197.255 ms. It is separate from the four fixed public admission samples; its request binds to the saved native-job intent and verified native selection.",
    "S90D reproduced a slow public managed job.forget: 1338.224 ms over HTTPS, with journal_begin 193.771 ms, worker 20.394 ms, journal_finish 1061.122 ms and handler 1283.631 ms. Most of this request elapsed in the two service journal phases.",
    "QN90A had two successful maintenance exec requests dominated by journal_finish: 1220.967 ms of a 1307.403 ms HTTPS request, and 1151.516 ms of a 1256.663 ms request. Worker phases were 26.273 and 34.229 ms. These observations locate these two delays in service result publication, not worker execution or surrounding local harness writes.",
    "Journal.finish performs a durable file publication with file sync, rename and parent-directory sync. Its phase also includes serialization and scheduling. The measurements do not isolate an individual syscall or prove a storage/writeback mechanism, and do not retroactively attribute older outliers.",
    "All executable/native/managed payload members are byte-identical to 0.7.46. The native manifest source list includes previously committed diagnostic source changes; its artifact entries are unchanged. Service api.js, version/signatures and manifest metadata changed."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Each implementation has four public job-admission and four forget samples per TV; medians and maxima are descriptive, not stable tail distributions. Historical latency outliers and the performance no-regression gate remain open.",
    "The service handler interval contains the measured phases and includes body receipt/validation/response preparation. It excludes earlier TLS setup and later response transmission; the remainder of host elapsed time is not pure network time.",
    "Only attempted phases are reported. Read-only calls omit journal metrics. Timed failures retain their original rejection/uncertainty semantics; outcomes and replay protection come from the durable journal, never timing headers.",
    "The reduced observer still has nonzero overhead and sparse mapping samples. Short-lived processes and peaks may be missed; this is not complete process-tree or endurance coverage.",
    "QN90A deployment acceptance disarmed the 300-second rescue about 26.948 seconds after its restore-intent file was written. Later extra cleanup found all deployment units unloaded/inactive, so a surviving service start counter was unavailable. S90D checks its zero start counter before disarming. Both integrated rounds independently verify their rescue start counters as zero.",
    "The first QN90A extra cleanup refused an already-unloaded timer. Read-only reconciliation proved every deployment timer/service absent and inactive before the check was updated to skip already-inactive timers. No install or uncertain worker request was replayed.",
    "No deliberate reboot/standby, global policy, persistent capability or SMACK change occurred. The managed acquisition bridge, worker fallback and independent .NET SDK rescue remain available. Native-only entry, broader lifecycle/resource/24-hour endurance and native-default observation remain unfinished."
  ]
}
